====

Understanding the name: ml.t3.medium

AWS instance names have a meaning:

ml . t3 . medium
│    │      │
│    │      └── Instance size
│    └──────── Instance family/type
└───────────── Machine Learning / SageMaker
1. ml

Means it is being used as a machine learning instance in SageMaker.

2. t3

The instance family.

t family is generally designed for lighter or variable CPU workloads.

3. medium

The size/capacity of the virtual computer.

For example:

t3.medium  → Smaller
t3.large   → More RAM
m5.large   → More powerful general-purpose
m5.2xlarge → Much more CPU + RAM

====

Main Instance Types
🟢 1. General Purpose — t3, t2, m5, m6

Used for normal workloads.

Python
Jupyter Notebook
Small datasets
Basic ML
Web applications

Examples:

ml.t3.medium
ml.t3.large
ml.m5.large

👉 Best for your current SageMaker learning: ml.t3.medium

====

🔵 2. Compute Optimized — c5, c6

More CPU power.

Used when your program needs heavy processing.

Large calculations
Data processing
ML training
CPU-intensive applications

Example:

ml.c5.large

Think:

More CPU power = faster calculations

=====

🟡 3. Memory Optimized — r5, r6

More RAM.

Used for:

Large datasets
Big Data
In-memory processing
Large ML workloads

Example:

ml.r5.large

Think:

More RAM = handle more data at one time

====

🔴 4. GPU Instances — g4, g5, p3, p4

These have GPU processors.

Used for:

Deep Learning
Neural Networks
Image Recognition
Computer Vision
Large AI Models
LLM training

Example:

ml.g5.xlarge

Think:

CPU → General processing
GPU → Thousands of calculations simultaneously

